    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d385">

                <pb facs="0538" n="524" xml:id="pg524"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.918/10–2445: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos Aires</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-10-24T21:00:00-03:00">October 24, 1945—9
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 25—1:03 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2649. ReEmbtel 2639 October 24. Have just been informed by Foreign Office that
                    last issue of <hi rendition="#italic">Time</hi> will not be released view of
                    fact it even goes into “private lives” and is “almost immoral”. I inquired
                    acidly whether this meant that Lomuto’s assurances were no longer valid; answer
                    was substantially in affirmative. Official made it clear that he was speaking
                    for Foreign Minister. Would appreciate instructions.<anchor n="36"
                        xml:id="d385-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d385-f1" n="36" xml:id="d385-f1-content">
                <p>In instruction 7166, November 9, 1945, the Chargé was informed that no official
                    protest need be made (835.918/11–245).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
